1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://runeberg.org/frfinl/0312.html
2 CONT
2 CONT INCONSISTENCIES AND GAPS IN GENI – ESPECIALLY REGARDING ANNA MARIA RITTERFELT GENANNT BYEN (BEIJ), ALSO KNOWN AS ANNA MARIA VON NANDELSTADT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Conflicting marriage information
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan von Nandelstadt († 1655) is historically confirmed to have lived in Joutseno, Finland, where he was granted fiefs. He was married to a woman named Anna Maria Ritterfelt genannt Byen.
2 CONT Ernst von Nandelstadt († 1665) had a military career in the Swedish army and served under Johan Lilljehöök’s regiment. His connection to Finland is less certain, but some sources name him as the husband of a woman named Anna Bye (
2 CONC Beij).
2 CONT The problem lies in the fact that both von Nandelstadt brothers are connected to what appears to be the same woman by name: Anna Maria Ritterfelt genannt Byen.
2 CONT Possible resolution: Johan was most likely the first husband, and Anna Maria became a widow in 1655. Theoretically, she could have married Johan’s brother Ernst later, if he moved to Finland. By then, Anna Maria might have been to
2 CONC o old to bear children. It is also possible that both brothers married daughters of Johan Ritterfelt genannt Byen—sisters—whose first names have been conflated. Some sources do refer to Ritterfelt’s daughters in the plural, but on
2 CONC ly this one is named.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Children and their parentage
2 CONT
2 CONT •	N.N. von Nandelstadt, who married Georg von Schildt: Her parentage is uncertain, but Johan is the more probable father, as he had stronger ties to Finland.
2 CONT •	Jost Vilhelm von Nandelstadt († 1707): Available sources identify him as the son of Ernst.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. The von Nandelstadts’ move to Finland
2 CONT
2 CONT The Swedish Crown distributed fiefs in exchange for military service.
2 CONT •	Johan von Nandelstadt was granted land in Joutseno in 1650.
2 CONT •	His presumed widow, Anna Maria, was mentioned in court records in 1655, likely related to estate division—suggesting her identity was confirmed in court.
2 CONT •	Ernst’s link to Finland is more uncertain, but he received two farms in Birkkala in 1657, which implies some presence in Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Interpretation of the lineage
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Johan von Nandelstadt was likely the father of N.N. von Nandelstadt, who became the wife of Georg von Schildt.
2 CONT •	Anna Maria, after being widowed, may have married Ernst, but this remains speculative without confirming documents. It’s also possible that Ernst’s wife was a sister of Anna Maria, and their names were confused.
2 CONT •	Jost Vilhelm is listed as Ernst’s son. He may have been from a second marriage with Magdalena Wartmann.
2 CONT 5. Recommendation for Geni
2 CONT •	Anna Maria Ritterfelt genannt Bye (Beij) should be listed as Johan’s wife.
2 CONT •	Ernst’s wife might have been a different Ritterfelt sister—possibly Anna Bye (Beij)—but not the same person as Johan’s wife.
2 CONT •	Johan’s daughter was most likely N.N. von Nandelstadt, who married Georg von Schildt.
2 CONT •	Jost Vilhelm von Nandelstadt was apparently Ernst’s son. Ernst also had a second wife, Magdalena Wartmann.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Sources and need for further research
2 CONT
2 CONT •	Project Runeberg – Frälsesläkter i Finland intill stora ofreden
2 CONT •	Project Runeberg – Den med sköldebref förlänade men ej å Riddarhuset introducerade svenska adelns ättar-taflor
2 CONT •	Anbytarforum Rötter. Svar #7: https://forum.rotter.se/index.php?topic=66552.msg947380#msg947380
2 CONT •	”Tuhat vuotta Karsturannan historiaa”. Kylän historiaprojekti 2020-21  (A Thousand Years of Karsturanta’s History (local history project): https://www.karsturanta.fi/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/Tuhat-vuotta-Karsturannan-historiaa
2 CONC .pdf
2 CONT •	Liite 2.4. Muukonsaaren asutus ja polut saaren halki (Appendix 2.4 – Settlement and trails across Muukonsaari): https://lab.fi/sites/default/files/2024-10/Liite_2_4_Muukonsaaren%20asutus_ja_polku.pdf
2 CONT •	Suku Forum: https://suku.genealogia.fi/archive/index.php/t-2009.html
2 CONT •	Geni.com – Anna Maria von Nandelstadt (Ritterfelt genannt Bye/Beij)
2 CONT •	Geni.com – N.N. Ernstdotter Schildt (N.N. von Nandelstadt) https://www.geni.com/people/N-N-von-Nandelstadt/5546205916350079760
