1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_Leszczy%C5%84ska_%281660%E2%80%931727%29 '''Anna Leszczyńska'''] - From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT * Anna Leszczyńska (1660–1727)
2 CONT * Coat of arms 	Prus III
2 CONT * Spouse(s) 	Rafał Leszczyński
2 CONT * Issue - Stanisław Leszczyński
2 CONT * Noble family -Jabłonowski
2 CONT * Father -Stanisław Jan Jabłonowski
2 CONT * Mother -Marianna Kazanowska
2 CONT * Born -1660
2 CONT * Kraków, Poland
2 CONT * Died - August 29, 1727 (aged 66–67),Chambord, Loir-et-Cher, France
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Anna Jabłonowska (1660–1727) was a Polish noble lady and the mother of King of Poland Stanisław I Leszczyński.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Hetman Stanisław Jan Jabłonowski and Marianna Kazanowska. In 1676, she married the son of Deputy Chancellor Boguslaw Leszczyński, the Grand Treasurer Rafał Leszczyński.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her son Stanisław Leszczyński became King of Poland and reigned from 1704 until 1709 and from 1733 until 1736.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ana_Jablonowska
