0 @N6000000002322288651@ NOTE The only son of a Polish noble, Stanislaw became a victim of foreign attempts
1 CONT to dominate Poland during a period of great problems and turmoil. Poland,
1 CONT weak and fragmented, had become a marching ground for foreign armies who
1 CONT ravaged the country at will. Augustus II, having been deposed in 1704 in
1 CONT favor of Stanislaw, regained the throne in 1709 and Stanislaw left the
1 CONT country to settle in the French Provence of Alsace. In 1725 his daughter
1 CONT Marie married King Louis XV of France.
